Analysing Android App Permissions and Mobile Traffic

Step 1: Install Android Studio
Download and install Android Studio
Launch the application

Step 2: Create Android Virtual Device (AVD)
Open AVD Manager
Click Create Virtual Device
Select device:
Pixel 2
Pixel 9
Select system image and finish setup

Step 3: Start the Emulator with Proxy
Open Command Prompt:
cd C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\emulator
emulator -list-avds
Example output:
Medium_Phone_API_36.1
Pixel_2
Pixel_9
Start emulator with proxy:
emulator -avd Pixel_9 -http-proxy http://10.0.2.2:8080

Step 4: Configure Proxy in Emulator (Manual Method)
In Emulator:
Settings → Network & Internet
Select Wi-Fi → Edit (pencil icon)
Advanced options
Proxy → Manual
Enter:
Hostname: 10.0.2.2
Port: 8080
Click Save

Step 5: Configure Proxy Using ADB (Alternative Method)
Open Command Prompt:
cd C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\platform-tools
adb devices
Expected:
emulator-5554 device
Set proxy:
adb shell settings put global http_proxy 10.0.2.2:8080
Verify:
adb shell settings get global http_proxy
Output:
10.0.2.2:8080

Step 6: Configure Burp Suite
Open Burp Suite
Go to Proxy → Options
Under Proxy Listeners → Edit
Select All interfaces
Set port: 8080
Enable:
Intercept ON

Step 7: Capture HTTP Traffic
In Emulator:
Open Chrome
Visit:
http://example.com
👉 In Burp Suite:
Go to Proxy → HTTP History
Observation:
HTTP requests and responses are visible

Step 8: Install Burp CA Certificate (for HTTPS)
Export Certificate from Burp:
Proxy → Options
Import/Export CA Certificate
Choose DER format
Save as:
burpcer.der

Step 9: Transfer Certificate to Emulator
adb push C:\Users\Admin\Downloads\burpcer.der /sdcard/Download/

Step 10: Install Certificate in Emulator
In Emulator:
Settings
→ Security & Privacy
→ More Security Settings
→ Encryption & Credentials
→ Install a certificate
→ CA Certificate
Select:
burpcer.der

Step 11: Verify HTTPS Interception
In Emulator:
Open Chrome
Visit:
https://example.com
In Burp Suite:
Check Proxy → HTTP History
Observation:
HTTPS requests and responses are now visible

